# Settings of ~/.pi/agent/settings.json that bin/save-settings copies into
# configs/pi/settings.json. A public rule names one setting. A private rule
# can name a whole section. Each key in configs/pi/settings.json needs a
# public rule. Settings on neither list are counted, not saved: run
# ./bin/save-settings --show-new to list them.
# Pi runs each command with `bash -c`, which reads no startup file. This prefix
# activates mise first, as zshenv does for the agents that run zsh.
public .shellCommandPrefix
